[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says: one issue, one fix queued. Read by cause instead of by subject
line, the reports merged into it are three problems. Each has its own fix, and each now has its
own ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
The queued parser fix does not close #4471. The booking-v3 hint and the one-day move stay broken
after it ships.
</Callout>

## The tickets

| problem in #4471 | in the table below | ticket |
|---|---|---|
| The shared parser reads every date month first | row `parser` | [jexor23/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows#1](https://github.com/jexor23/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1) |
| booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` for day-first tenants | row `hint` | [jexor23/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows#2](https://github.com/jexor23/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2) |
| Dates move one day earlier | the note under the table: reports read as a one-day move | [jexor23/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows#4](https://github.com/jexor23/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/4) |

Each ticket carries how many reports it covers and their ids. No report is in two tickets: the
parser ticket counts the `parser` row without the one-day moves from the note under the table.

## What #4471 holds

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The table counts each report id once: the ticket export pages overlap, so some reports come
twice. A report's cause comes from its tenant (locale and booking form), not from intake's tag,
which is a guess from the reporter's browser; the "tagged as" column shows how often they differ.
The one-day moves stay filed under `parser` by tenant in this table; they have their own ticket.

## 1 · `parser`: the shared parser reads dates month first

Every tenant on file writes the day first. The shared parser reads every date month first, so any
date with a day of 12 or less comes out with day and month swapped: "Booked for 7 April. The
invite says 4 July." It reaches the desk through the app, email and booking-v2 forms of all
tenants. Fix: parse with the tenant's locale, not a fixed month-first order.
Ticket: [#1](https://github.com/jexor23/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1).

## 2 · `hint`: booking-v3 tells day-first tenants to type the month first

booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People at the day-first tenants that run it
type what the hint says, month first, and the form reads the date the tenant's way, day first.
The symptom is the same swap as the parser's, so the subject lines match and decision 0001
merged them. The cause is the form, not the parser: the parser fix does not touch it. Only
reports sent through the booking-v3 form belong here. Fix: print the hint from the tenant's
locale (`DD/MM/YYYY` for these tenants), as booking-v2 does.
Ticket: [#2](https://github.com/jexor23/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2).

## 3 · one-day move: dates move one day earlier

These are not swaps. "Invite says Tuesday 12 May. Calendar says Monday 11 May." "Tuesday
6 October showed as Monday." "Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday. Same
meeting." The date moves back one day, and which day a reader sees depends on where they are.
That points to a date-only value converted through a time zone (stored or sent as midnight UTC,
shown in local time), not to the date order. Neither the parser fix nor the hint fix touches it.
The desk had already read these as one-day moves (`desk-notes.json`). R-41236 ("the invite
arrived before I made the booking") has no dates in it; it stays here with the desk's reading.
Ticket: [#4](https://github.com/jexor23/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/4).

## What this means for the desk

- #4471 stays open only for `parser`. The other two problems are tracked in their own tickets.
- Decision 0001 merges by subject line. These three problems share subject lines, so the rule put
  them in one ticket. Decision 0001 is accepted and is not edited here; a new decision record
  should replace it with "merge when the cause is the same", which `DedupeExplorer` already
  computes.
- Intake's tags do not decide a problem. The "tagged as" column shows how often they disagree
  with the cause.

